{%- comment -%}
  Judge.me preview badge — the star rating and review count.

  Judge.me is installed as a theme app extension (handle `judgeme-657`,
  widget version 3.0). The badge is hydrated client-side by the app's
  loader, but Judge.me also writes a server-rendered copy into
  `product.metafields.judgeme.badge`. Emitting that metafield inside the
  hydration target means the rating is in the initial HTML — good for
  SEO and for users on slow connections — and is then replaced in place
  once the app's script runs.

  ⚠ INTEGRATION POINTS ARE SACRED
  The class `jdgm-widget jdgm-preview-badge` and the `data-id` attribute
  are what the Judge.me loader looks for. Renaming either silently
  breaks every rating on the site. Do not "tidy" them.

  ⚠ NOT VERIFIED AGAINST A LIVE STORE
  This repository has no store credentials, so this snippet has been
  written from the audit rather than tested against a running Judge.me
  install. Confirm it renders before relying on it.
  Source: reference-analysis/06-REVIEWS.md §4.

  WHY REVIEWS STAY LOUD
  4.98★ from 1,212 reviews (live, 2026-08-12) is the store's strongest
  competitive asset. DIRECTION.md Part 1 §2.1 is explicit that Amouage's
  review restraint must NOT be copied — they sell at $395, Siwa at ~$19.
  No caller may hide this badge to tidy a layout.

  Accepts:
    product  {Product}  required
    class    {String}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if product != blank -%}
  <div
    class="jdgm-widget jdgm-preview-badge {{ class }}"
    data-id="{{ product.id }}"
    data-template="{{ template.name | default: 'index' }}"
  >
    {{- product.metafields.judgeme.badge -}}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
